  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This makes 6 portions and takes about 1 hour 20 minutes including steaming. The thing to watch is the batter consistency: it should pour easily but not be watery. Too thick and it will not cook evenly through the centre; too thin and it will not set."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Wrap each portion in a doubled layer of foil if not using banana leaves. The steam needs to be kept inside each parcel to cook the batter properly. Loose wrapping means steam escapes and the centre stays soft."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 6,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "black-eyed-beans",
              "amount": 400,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "soaked overnight, drained and peeled",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "pepper-red",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "large",
